From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] md: clear CHANGE_PENDING for dm-raid without metadata

A dm-raid set without metadata devices is non-persistent and external
(dm-raid.c), and md_update_sb() only clears MD_SB_CHANGE_PENDING for a
non-persistent array that is not external (an external one has its
metadata handler, mdmon, do it). md_do_sync() sets that flag at the end
of every sync (resync, check, repair): nothing ever cleared it, raid5d
stopped at the top of its loop for good, and every write submitted to
the RAID 4/5/6 afterwards hung, reads still working. Seen on the NAS
with a dm-raid raid5_la, no metadata: the first write after "sync" or
"check" never completed (jbd2 and sync in D state, raid5d asleep).
Clear it for a dm array too: there is nobody else to.
---
--- a/drivers/md/md.c
+++ b/drivers/md/md.c
@@ -2842,7 +2842,10 @@
 	if (!mddev->persistent) {
 		clear_bit(MD_SB_CHANGE_CLEAN, &mddev->sb_flags);
 		clear_bit(MD_SB_CHANGE_DEVS, &mddev->sb_flags);
-		if (!mddev->external) {
+		/* dm-raid without metadata devices is external too, but has no
+		 * metadata handler to clear CHANGE_PENDING (set by md_do_sync()
+		 * at the end of every sync): raid5d would wait for it forever */
+		if (!mddev->external || mddev_is_dm(mddev)) {
 			clear_bit(MD_SB_CHANGE_PENDING, &mddev->sb_flags);
 			rdev_for_each(rdev, mddev) {
 				if (rdev->badblocks.changed) {
